					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-09-10 | Monday</font></strong><br><br><div style="text-align: center"><img src="http://a897.ac-images.myspacecdn.com/images01/123/m_ffc4ad8af959f7865225ea8f98e1e4c8.jpg" alt="" /></div><br /><div style="text-align: center"><img src="http://a455.ac-images.myspacecdn.com/images01/117/m_bbc81da1779088e04097a214dc67875e.jpg" alt="" /></div><br />i think we&#39;re gonna increase the amount of downloads we make available.  every <strong>monday</strong> and <strong>thursday</strong>, keep checkin back with us.<br /><br />today we have a cut from the <strong>Balance Brothers</strong>, better known to some as <strong>Khingz Makoma</strong> of <strong>Abyssinian Creole</strong>, and <strong>Nam</strong> from... um, Beacon Hill.  check it out.  this is for the cops.<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-09-05 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br><br /><object width="425" height="350" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" data="http://www.youtube.com/v/i-hXNi1DCAM"><param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/hXNi1DCAM"></param><br /><param name="wmode" value="transparent"></param><br /></object><br /><br /><br /><br />Got a call at 1pm that <strong>Ryan Shaw </strong>had an unfortunate airplane mishap that was gonna prevent him from performing at the 745pm slot at Bumbershoot. I was already going to be in attendance for the homie <strong>Gabriel Teodros</strong>&#39; set, and with my dudes <strong>Khingz</strong> and <strong>Macklemore</strong> also present, I figured... let&#39;s rock a <strong>Good Medicine</strong> set! Then, I hit up Sabzi to come through and we ended up doing a last-minute fill-in <strong>Blue Scholars </strong>set feat. the Medicine men. <br /><br />Word spread quickly and towards the end of the set, we invited a handful of 206 representatives chillin backstage to rock what ended up being a spontaneous 8-minute version of North By Northwest with freestyles blessed by (in order): <br /><br /><strong>Tilson (The Saturday Knights), <br />Asun (Alpha-P), </strong><br />Macklemore<strong>, <br />Xperience, <br />Language Arts, <br />Toni Hill, <br />Gatsby (Cancer Rising), <br />Jerm (Alpha-P), <br />Rufio, <br />Grynch, <br />Nam </strong>and <br />Khingz<strong>. <br /><br /></strong>It truly has been the summer of Northwest hip-hop. If you were there, you witnessed a &quot;moment.&quot; If you weren&#39;t, peep the video!<br /><br />geo<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-09-03 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>check out the NEW DOWNLOAD TO YOUR UPPER RIGHT.<br /><br />Townfolk at it again.<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-08-31 | Friday</font></strong><br><br>It goes down tonight at the <strong>War Room</strong>! The Seattle installation of the Big Tune beat battle, put on by <strong>J. Moore and Vitamin D</strong>. 12 production teams/individuals go head to head, showcasing their hottest beats for the title of Seattle&#39;s best beatmaker. I&#39;ve already heard some heat from <strong>MTK</strong> (don&#39;t sleep yall) and the rest of the lineup looks formidable. And of course I&#39;m biased but I really don&#39;t think folks are ready for what I&#39;ve heard <strong>Sabzi</strong> cooking up the past few days - on the road, no less! Oh, and <strong>Dyme Def</strong> and <strong>J. Pinder</strong> will be performing. Aaaand, <strong>DJ DV One</strong> will be the selector for the evening. All for $5!<br /><br />Here&#39;s the complete lineup:<br /><br />Bean One<br />Black and Brown<br />Bleek Beats<br />Brainstorm<br />Budo<br />DJ Nphared<br />Eric G<br />J Keys<br />MTK<br />Ra Charm Music<br />Sabzi<br />Smoke<br /><br />Go check www.redbullbigtune.com for more info. <br /><br />FRIDAY<br />AUGUST 31, 2007<br />BIG TUNE BEAT BATTLE @ WAR ROOM<br />722 E Pike, Seattle, WA<br />Doors 9pm | $5 (21+)<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-08-29 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br>this show was kinda nuts.&nbsp; got to see Hieroglyphics for the first time altogether.&nbsp; that was a treat. <br /><br />peace to the homies at <strong>AMFM</strong>, and many thanks to folks at <strong>Exact Science</strong>, <strong>The Originators</strong>, and <strong>Orisue</strong> for the gear!<br /><br />... and of course, the homegirl Lauren at Sony for being such a sweetheart. =)<br /><br />looks like we&#39;re late this week on the free download, but it was well worth the wait.&nbsp; this week&#39;s cut is another track from the lost MassLine Mixtape.&nbsp; it&#39;s called <strong>&quot;Hold Up&quot;</strong> with <strong>RA Scion</strong> and <strong>Chev</strong>, with <strong>Infinote</strong> on the beat.<br /><br />bump it!<br /><br />saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> [19] <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=245">[50]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=250">[51]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=255">[52]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=260">[53]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=265">[54]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=270">[55]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=275">[56]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=280">[57]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=285">[58]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=290">[59]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[&gt;&gt;]</A>  </span></p>
